  "allele.forestry.bee_species.binniebees.arid": "Arid",
  "allele.forestry.bee_species.binniebees.arid.desc": "Fond of dry landscapes, their combs are quite waxy and contain less honey.|Apiarist Manual",
  "allele.forestry.bee_species.binniebees.barren": "Barren",
  "allele.forestry.bee_species.binniebees.barren.desc": "Preferring deserts, they can live their entire lives without seeing flowers of any kind.|Apiarist Manual",
  "allele.forestry.bee_species.binniebees.desolate": "Desolate",
  "allele.forestry.bee_species.binniebees.desolate.desc": "They thrive in blasted wastelands where other life simply withers away.|Apiarist Manual",
  "allele.forestry.bee_species.binniebees.decomposing": "Decomposing",
  "allele.forestry.bee_species.binniebees.gnawing": "Gnawing",
  "allele.forestry.bee_species.binniebees.rotten": "Decaying",
  "allele.forestry.bee_species.binniebees.rotten.desc": "These bees have an unusual attraction to dead, rotting meat and will store it in their combs. The smell also attracts other unsavoury types.|Apiarist Manual",
  "allele.forestry.bee_species.binniebees.bone": "Skeletal",
  "allele.forestry.bee_species.binniebees.bone.desc": "Largely unable to defend their hives in the wild, they attract other creatures to guard their homes.|Apiarist Manual",
  "allele.forestry.bee_species.binniebees.creeper": "Creepy",
  "allele.forestry.bee_species.binniebees.creeper.desc": "You're sure to get a bang out of these bees.|Binnie, Apiarist",
  "allele.forestry.bee_species.binniebees.rock": "Rocky",
  "allele.forestry.bee_species.binniebees.rock.desc": "If only I could find them Rolling Bees, then I might get some good music.|Mysterious Apiarist",
  "allele.forestry.bee_species.binniebees.stone": "Tolerant",
  "allele.forestry.bee_species.binniebees.stone.desc": "Part of their hive is made out of stone and use less wax than before.|Apiarist Manual",
  "allele.forestry.bee_species.binniebees.granite": "Robust",
  "allele.forestry.bee_species.binniebees.granite.desc": "Capable of burrowing through solid rock, they have an extraordinary affinity for minerals hidden in rocks.|Apiarist Manual",
  "allele.forestry.bee_species.binniebees.mineral": "Resilient",
  "allele.forestry.bee_species.binniebees.mineral.desc": "Generations of breeding Rocky bees and their offspring has resulted in offspring that have begun to consume minerals as part of their diet.|Apiarist Manual",
  "allele.forestry.bee_species.binniebees.copper": "Corroded",
